1 NAME Michael /Brady/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1890
2 PLAC Drumbar, Cavan
1 NOTE Birth year is an estimate, worked back from the children's ages (Gretta b. c.1920s), not from a record
1 NOTE Farmer of Drumbar, Cavan; named as Margaret (Gretta) Brady's father on her 1949 marriage record
1 NOTE Re-reading the 1949 register: Drumbar, Cavan is Gretta's address as a domestic servant at the time of her marriage — her place of work, not necessarily her home. Michael's own townland is not given, so he could be anywhere in Cavan district
1 NOTE Gretta is not in the 1926 census under Margaret or Gretta Brady, so she was born after April 1926; her birth record will not be public until the 2030s
1 NOTE Of the Michael Bradys who married in Cavan district 1920–35, the nearest in place is Michael Brady of Drumcor (Drung), who married Rose Anne Fitzpatrick, a national-school teacher of Ballinagh, at Drumcor on 17 August 1927 — his father Bern
1 SOUR
2 TITL Civil marriage, Thomas Galligan and Margaret Brady, Cathedral of SS Patrick and Felim, Cavan, 21 Feb 1949 (Cavan district, entry 110)
2 NOTE https://www.irishgenealogy.ie/view/?record_id=cima-1077980
1 SOUR
2 TITL Census 1901, 1911 and 1926, Drumbar, Crossdoney DED, Co. Cavan: James Brady (60, farmer) and Alice (35) with daughters in 1901; Alice a widow with Rose, Maggie and Maria in 1911; Alice, 65, widow, alone in 1926
2 NOTE https://www.census.nationalarchives.ie/pages/1911/Cavan/Crossdoney/Drumbar/
