1 NAME Terence /McCormack/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1841
2 PLAC Corbally and Hammondstown, Fore, Co. Westmeath
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1901
1 NOTE Registered son James's birth himself in March 1876 as 'Terence McCormac, farmer, Hilltown', signing with his mark
1 NOTE The 1909 marriage record names James's father as 'Thos. McCormack' — a clerk's slip for Terence, since the father's own 1876 registration, the townland and the mother all match
1 NOTE Census 1901: Terence McCormack, 60, married, at Corbally (house 5) with his sister Bridget, 40 — while his wife Catherine ran the Hammondstown farm. Corbally was the family's home place; James's son Andy farmed it until 1991
1 NOTE Griffith's Valuation (c.1854, under Fore's old parish name St Feighin) has Michael, Anne and John McCormick holding land at Corbally — Terence, born c.1841, grew up among them and one of the men is almost certainly his father
1 SOUR
