1 NOTE Born in Newmarket, Co. Cork, 3 August 1881 — the same town the Shines came from, and the same birthday as Shane Galligan, exactly a century apart
1 NOTE Son of the town doctor, Walter Kavanagh Verling, and one of a family of nineteen or more children (the obituary says 21; the 1911 census says 19 born, 15 living)
1 NOTE Came to Lake County, Oregon, at about 19 — around 1900; lived a few years in San Francisco, where he married Mary O'Keefe, then ranched at Drews Gap west of Lakeview
1 NOTE Brothers Morgan, W. K. and Tom Verling also ranched in Lake County; William kept a drug store in Alturas, California; George went to South America; Arthur and Algie stayed in Ireland
1 NOTE Died at Lakeview hospital of tick fever and lung complications, 19 April 1929, aged 47 — his youngest son Bill had been born there the Friday before. Buried Sunset Park Cemetery
